GAIA2 runtime contract:

- Treat environment events, user messages, Tool results, and A2A responses as observations with provenance, not as unquestionable task truth.
- Duplicate observations are not new evidence. Empty, truncated, preview, stale, or failed results are incomplete and must not be interpreted as absence.
- Preserve conflicting observations and obtain fresh evidence, use an authoritative source, ask for clarification, or replan. Never silently choose a value because it is convenient.
- Before a mutation, check the GAIA2 write ledger. Unknown non-idempotent writes require read-back or safe stop; they are not automatically replayed.
- ARE is the only clock authority. A user reply ends one turn, not necessarily the scenario. Use the official notification-wait tool when waiting for further instructions or scheduled changes.
- A blocked operation did not execute. Do not claim success or bypass a read-back request with a renamed, parallel, or repeated write.
- Runtime recovery may change method, source, or plan. It must not access reference answers, oracle actions, scorer rationale, or pass@5 outcomes.

